Voltdeck decodes the Bluetooth Low Energy protocols of third-party equipment.
Protocol knowledge comes from manufacturer documentation and from the Apache-2.0,
MIT, BSD-3-Clause and Unlicense projects listed below. No source code from these
projects is copied: decoders are rewritten in Kotlin from their specifications.
Test vectors taken from them are credited in the file that uses them.

  - Victron Energy, "Extra manufacturer Data" (2022-12-14), Instant Readout advertisements
  - patman15/aiobmsble and patman15/BMS_BLE-HA (Apache-2.0), JBD protocol
  - syssi/esphome-jbd-bms (Apache-2.0), JBD protocol
  - sshoecraft/jbdtool (BSD-3-Clause), JBD register map
  - rajlaud/victron-ble-ha-parser (Apache-2.0), keshavdv/victron-ble (Unlicense), Victron reference vectors

Victron, Ultimatron and Jiabaida are trademarks of their respective owners. They are
mentioned only to state which equipment Voltdeck is compatible with. Voltdeck is not
